NNAAMMEE
       sysfs - a filesystem for exporting kernel objects

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The ssyyssffss filesystem is a pseudo‐filesystem which provides an interface
       to  kernel data structures.  (More precisely, the files and directories
       in ssyyssffss provide a view of the _k_o_b_j_e_c_t  structures  defined  internally
       within  the  kernel.)   The files under ssyyssffss provide information about
       devices, kernel modules, filesystems, and other kernel components.

       The ssyyssffss filesystem is commonly mounted at  _/_s_y_s.   Typically,  it  is
       mounted  automatically  by the system, but it can also be mounted manu‐
       ally using a command such as:

           mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys

       Many of the files in the ssyyssffss filesystem are read‐only, but some files
       are writable, allowing kernel variables to be changed.  To avoid redun‐
       dancy, symbolic links are heavily used to connect  entries  across  the
       filesystem tree.

